From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 21:40:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rk3566-pinetab2: connect the rear camera

The PineTab2's rear camera never worked. The sensor itself is described and
probes fine - the ov5648 binds on i2c2 along with its dw9714 focus coil:

    2-0036: name=ov5648  driver=ov5648
    2-000c: name=dw9714  driver=dw9714

but its output goes nowhere. The endpoint carries a null phandle:

        port {
                endpoint {
                        data-lanes = <1 2>;
                        remote-endpoint = <0>;
                        link-frequencies = /bits/ 64 <210000000 168000000>;
                };
        };

so no media graph is ever formed. The only /dev/media devices on the running
tablet belong to the video codec, and libcamera lists no cameras at all:

    video0: rockchip-rga   video1: rk3568-vpu-dec   video2: rk3568-vepu-enc
    media0, media1: hantro-vpu

    $ cam -l
    Available cameras:
    (none)

On rk3566 the capture path is not the rkisp1 that the PinePhone Pro uses -
rk356x has no ISP node, only a qos_isp QoS entry - but VICAP, reached through
a Synopsys MIPI CSI-2 receiver:

    ov5648 -> csi@fdfb0000 -> video-capture@fdfe0000

Neither end of that existed in the device tree. video-capture@fdfe0000 is
present but disabled and its MIPI port has no endpoint, and rk356x-base.dtsi
has no CSI-2 receiver node at all, even though the binding
(rockchip,rk3568-mipi-csi2.yaml) and the driver
(drivers/media/platform/synopsys/dw-mipi-csi2rx.c) both cover rk3568. Add the
receiver from the binding's own rk3568 example, join it to vicap's MIPI port,
and leave it disabled for boards that do not use it.

The board then only has to switch the chain on and point the sensor at the
receiver. csi_dphy was already enabled here, which is what made the omission
easy to miss.

Pairs with CONFIG_VIDEO_ROCKCHIP_CIF and CONFIG_VIDEO_DW_MIPI_CSI2RX in
extra.cfg; both drivers were built out.

Only the rear sensor is wired. The front camera is not described in this DTS
at all beyond its pinctrl entries, so it stays unavailable.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
diff -ruN dts_a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2.dtsi dts_b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2.dtsi
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@
 #include <dt-bindings/input/gpio-keys.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/input/input.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/leds/common.h>
+#include <dt-bindings/media/video-interfaces.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/pinctrl/rockchip.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/soc/rockchip,vop2.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/usb/pd.h>
@@ -276,6 +277,22 @@
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+&csi {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&csi_in {
+	csi_input: endpoint {
+		bus-type = <MEDIA_BUS_TYPE_CSI2_DPHY>;
+		data-lanes = <1 2>;
+		remote-endpoint = <&ov5648_out>;
+	};
+};
+
+&vicap {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 &dsi0 {
 	status = "okay";
 	clock-master;
@@ -612,9 +629,10 @@
 		reset-gpios = <&gpio4 RK_PB1 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 
 		port {
-			endpoint {
+			ov5648_out: endpoint {
+				bus-type = <MEDIA_BUS_TYPE_CSI2_DPHY>;
 				data-lanes = <1 2>;
-				remote-endpoint = <0>;
+				remote-endpoint = <&csi_input>;
 				link-frequencies = /bits/ 64 <210000000 168000000>;
 			};
 		};
diff -ruN dts_a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk356x-base.dtsi dts_b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk356x-base.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk356x-base.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk356x-base.dtsi
@@ -639,6 +639,36 @@
 		#iommu-cells = <0>;
 	};
 
+	csi: csi@fdfb0000 {
+		compatible = "rockchip,rk3568-mipi-csi2";
+		reg = <0x0 0xfdfb0000 0x0 0x10000>;
+		interrupts = <GIC_SPI 8 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
+			     <GIC_SPI 9 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+		interrupt-names = "err1", "err2";
+		clocks = <&cru PCLK_CSI2HOST1>;
+		phys = <&csi_dphy>;
+		power-domains = <&power RK3568_PD_VI>;
+		resets = <&cru SRST_P_CSI2HOST1>;
+		status = "disabled";
+
+		ports {
+			#address-cells = <1>;
+			#size-cells = <0>;
+
+			csi_in: port@0 {
+				reg = <0>;
+			};
+
+			csi_out: port@1 {
+				reg = <1>;
+
+				csi_output: endpoint {
+					remote-endpoint = <&vicap_mipi_input>;
+				};
+			};
+		};
+	};
+
 	vicap: video-capture@fdfe0000 {
 		compatible = "rockchip,rk3568-vicap";
 		reg = <0x0 0xfdfe0000 0x0 0x200>;
@@ -667,6 +697,10 @@
 
 			vicap_mipi: port@1 {
 				reg = <1>;
+
+				vicap_mipi_input: endpoint {
+					remote-endpoint = <&csi_output>;
+				};
 			};
 		};
 	};
